comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-20T13:16:11.875Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete 2786-item all-status title inventory and live open/in-progress inventory contain no active September 20 compatible refresh. Current registry peer contracts exclude TypeScript 7 and Vitest 5; npm-package-arg 14 exceeds supported Node 22.18.0 floor. Existing canonical owners are reused as decision provenance."
  "2026-09-20T13:26:22.572Z","harness:codex","Applied compatible registry releases through pnpm with normal supply-chain policies: ESLint 10.11.0, Unicorn 76.0.0, Greptile 3.5.3 and Node declarations 26.6.2. Retained public @types/node >=22 and unchanged Node runtime floor. Current upstream typescript-eslint peer range is >=4.8.4 <6.1.0; CodSpeed accepts Vitest ^3.2 or ^4; npm-package-arg 14 requires Node ^22.22.2 or newer supported major floors. Canonical incompatible migrations remain open and unclaimed."
  "2026-09-20T13:42:35.002Z","harness:codex","After the compatible update, repository ESLint, typecheck and zero-clone duplication checks passed. pnpm outdated now contains only the existing incompatible major migrations; full audit remains zero vulnerabilities. Final static, serialized linked-test and full exact-coverage verdicts remain pending."
  "2026-09-20T13:47:29.999Z","harness:codex",Tracker-context assurance rejected growth of generic related edges. Removed the two incidental co-delivery links and retained typed discovered_from migration provenance plus implements the quality epic. No graph threshold or historical relationship was weakened.
  "2026-09-20T14:30:55.157Z","harness:codex","Repository static chain passed ESLint, duplicate checks, generated contracts, source-quality, package and command boundaries, token budgets, tracker quality, gate registry and SDK import costs. The initial transport-floor check exceeded latency limits; an isolated rerun passed all six operations without threshold changes. The remaining graph-composition and record-integrity checks passed. Serial linked tooling checks remain green."
  "2026-09-20T14:35:20.089Z","harness:codex","Live observability verification: required Sentry/telemetry gate passes with no blocking Sentry issues, 1.76% finish error rate and zero missing-error-code rows. A separate 15-minute production query observed 108 command_start, 107 command_finish and 4 command_error events, with latest finish at 2026-09-20T14:34:22Z; the physical event queue had zero ready or unacknowledged messages. Sentry had no unresolved issues seen in 24 hours, no one-hour trace rows, and its latest seven-day issue was already resolved. These are distinct receipts, not a claim that every possible user action has been exhaustively observed."
  "2026-09-20T14:37:50.245Z","harness:codex","Additional production correlation receipt: the recent 15-minute window contains 100 session/command start-finish pairs and zero starts older than two minutes without a corresponding finish. Only aggregate counts were retained; no raw user payloads or identifiers were copied into project records."
  "2026-09-20T14:48:36.011Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence: 9150 tests in 720 files pass. Exact source coverage is statements 64773/64773; branches 49459/49459; functions 13462/13462; lines 61981/61981, with zero skipped coverage. Native Bash 3.2 regression, serial linked tests, temporary-workspace lifecycle, installed helper transport, native Fish/Zsh acceptance and packed npm/npx/bunx smoke pass. Existing thresholds and exclusions were not weakened. GitHub review and CI will validate the submitted delivery head."
  "2026-09-20T14:51:18.494Z","harness:codex","Closeout verification: GitHub reports zero open Dependabot, code-scanning and secret-scanning alerts. Latest pm-changelog 2026.9.18 generated the three completed implementation entries under Unreleased, preserving the already published 2026.9.20 section. Terminal defect evidence has zero findings; tracker resolution/history-drift validation and documentation-link checks pass."
  "2026-09-20T14:52:55.686Z","harness:codex","Reviewed delivery: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1281 combines the implementation, regression coverage, package-generated changelog and recorded local evidence. Hosted checks and review findings are attached to the PR head; no published release is claimed for these Unreleased changes."
